{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYHPxuLPJyWubhogcwL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The two sides in In re: OpenAI, Inc. Copyright Infringement Litigation have taken positions that leave little room between them. The case combines 12 lawsuits, including The New York Times Co. v. Microsoft and OpenAI, which the Times filed in 2023. The Times alleges that OpenAI and Microsoft's use of its content for any purpose, including model training, violates copyright law. OpenAI and Microsoft respond that training and deploying models on publicly available data is technological development within fair use. Each side's position covers the whole pipeline, from training through the deployed product.\n\nThe Wikimedia Foundation's amicus brief, filed October 30, divides that pipeline. It argues that training an LLM that is something new and different from its sources should be fair use without any requirement to meet licensing terms. It argues the opposite for retrieval-augmented generation and newer grounding techniques, which the article describes as finding and copying works from the web and delivering that same content back to users through a chatbot. For those uses, Wikimedia says, companies should follow each publisher's licensing requirements.\n\nThe court's ruling could matter beyond this docket. Wikimedia notes that only a few cases have addressed the issue so far and that the jurisdiction and parties make this ruling highly influential for other courts. If that holds, how the court treats the stages of an AI system as one question or several could shape later cases. The brief is an argument offered to the court, and the article gives no indication yet of whether the court will adopt any part of it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1027,"cache_read_input_tokens":5926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1027},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cf95dce-9255-429f-a813-98c096d73638","uuid":"98428979-0599-443b-93b5-2f3f685d742c","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:21:37.094Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYHPkWwYYaozDtCLctG"}
